From: Cage maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] store: ignore Windows PID files whose PIDs were reused

Compare process creation time with the PID file's write time, allowing for
FAT timestamp rounding. Fall back to a system process snapshot when handle
queries fail, including for inaccessible processes. Keep markers when the
creation time cannot be established, and leave stale files to the next writer.
Release process handles and log ignored or exited PID files. Cover reused
PIDs, live owners without boot markers, and snapshot creation times in tests.

